  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "In and out – curved skate, pass and shot",
  "description": "Two lines with pucks along the sides, and a cone on each side a little way in towards goal. The lines take turns. A skates in a curve inwards past the cone and gets a pass from B. A receives, takes the puck past the cone and shoots. Then D skates from the other side and gets the pass from E.\n\nIt matters that the sides do not go too close together, so the goalkeeper has time to move between shots. The players swap lines after their shot. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The curved skate should go inwards – then you arrive facing the goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The passer plays the puck in front of the skater."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Wait until the goalkeeper is set before the next player starts."
    }
  ],
